{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Honor</b> — that the king will honor the man who withdraws, if he sits and keeps quiet from strife; therefore the lamed has a kamatz, for it is definite, namely he who withdraws with him." "<b>Will reveal himself</b> — will involve himself in strife."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {0 "The Hebrew לאיש המתעבר seems grammatically difficult; translated hyper-literally. The kamatz reference is to the vowel under the lamed of לאיש in the lemma."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:46.458641659Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}